      "mobile": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"100%\" style=\"height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 460\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"nv5-justice-en-mobile-title nv5-justice-en-mobile-desc\" xml:lang=\"en\" data-kind=\"justice\" data-variant=\"mobile\"><title id=\"nv5-justice-en-mobile-title\">Documents and judicial oversight</title><desc id=\"nv5-justice-en-mobile-desc\">A general diagram of US federal procedure, not an assignment of procedural status to any particular case. In civil antitrust, a civil investigative demand gathers records; an action or settlement can then go before a court, which rules on remedies. In criminal proceedings, subpoenaed material can be considered by a grand jury; a possible charge leads to proceedings before a judge. Solid links represent evidence gathering; dotted links represent possible subsequent steps. A document demand and a final decision occupy different stages.</desc><rect x=\"1\" y=\"1\" width=\"398\" height=\"458\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"var(--color-surface)\" stroke=\"var(--color-line-strong)\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"30\" font-family=\"l0g Nvidia State Leverage\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"var(--color-paper)\" data-zone=\"header\">Documents and judicial oversight</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"55\" font-family=\"l0g Nvidia State Leverage\" font-size=\"17.5\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"var(--color-muted)\" data-zone=\"header\">Federal procedure · general framework</text><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"72\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"443\" stroke=\"var(--color-line-strong)\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"105\" y=\"82\" font-family=\"l0g Nvidia State Leverage\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"var(--color-signal)\" data-zone=\"channel\">Civil antitrust</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"82\" font-family=\"l0g Nvidia State Leverage\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"var(--color-amber