    "project": {
      "desktop": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"100%\" style=\"height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 800 420\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"nv5-project-en-desktop-title nv5-project-en-desktop-desc\" xml:lang=\"en\" data-kind=\"project\" data-variant=\"desktop\"><title id=\"nv5-project-en-desktop-title\">MP Materials: funding and contractual consent rights</title><desc id=\"nv5-project-en-desktop-desc\">Historical example: the July 2025 agreement between MP Materials and the Pentagon. Commitments include an initial $400 million preferred investment, a $150 million loan commitment, and purchase and price-support agreements. These instruments fund or support the group; the loan concerns Mountain Pass while the production offtake concerns the 10X facility. The specified period during which certain Pentagon consents are required continues if a defined securities-holding condition is met, or if purchase or price-support contracts remain in force, or if the loan remains unpaid. The OR operator represents these alternative conditions. The consent rights cover defined asset and change-of-control transactions. The mechanism is presented as a historical MP Materials precedent.</desc><rect x=\"1\" y=\"1\" width=\"798\" height=\"418\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"var(--color-surface)\" stroke=\"var(--color-line-strong)\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"33\" font-family=\"l0g Nvidia State Leverage\" font-size=\"22\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"var(--color-paper)\" data-zone=\"header\">MP Materials: funding and contractual consent rights</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"61\" font-family=\"l0g Nvidia State Leverage\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"400\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"var(--color-muted)\" data-zone=\"header\">July 2025 agreement · historical example</text><path d=\"M58 128L85 112L112 128Z\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--color-paper)\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><line x1=\"58\" y1=\"133\" x2=\"112\" y2=\"1